text:
[The text appears to be a treatise on medieval astrology, discussing the relationships of planets to zodiac signs, their triplicities (fire, earth, air, water groupings), degrees, dignities, and influences of Saturn, Jupiter, Mars, Venus, Mercury, and the Moon. Much of the specific wording is obscured by heavy scribal abbreviation and is not reliably legible; what follows is a general sense of the content.]

The greater [dignity] belongs to the planet [when it is] in its triplicity, and in fire [sign] and Sagittarius, which [is] in the fiery triplicity, and the Moon in Pisces and Scorpio ... through its course the planet is in its triplicity, which is in the first degree, the almuten [ruler].

It has also triplicity in some sign, two [signs] being as it were in its own house, as in Aries and Sagittarius, and likewise in Capricorn, giving it its own figure/place.

Likewise for Gemini, whatever sign [one examines], up to 30 degrees, and beyond that, in another manner, it equals whatever portion/term there is, up to 3 degrees, immediately it takes [its lord].

As the planet is in its own term, in the first/second degree it bears Mars['s]; in the term of the first degree [through] certain degrees [it] holds the term; then it changes to another, degree by degree, to another term, [and] so continues; Mercury and the Sun [also have] their own terms.

Likewise the degrees of their houses, degree by degree, continue through their own [limits], and so for the Moon, Saturn also.

Concerning these things, let it not be said that the fixed stars are to be reduced/followed, except when the aspect is made, [as is] shown in 80 planetary configurations, [or] in the fixed ones which are so reduced according to the sign which [governs] them; let him follow it accordingly.

[Below the table:]

It is true that some write otherwise, that is, that this planet precedes, I know, that which
in [the] 24th degree of Mars, the 3rd of the Sun, in the degree of Venus, 1, this is Jupiter['s] ... this Moon, and
then showing Saturn in its own [house], in the 2nd house, this end of the planet [is placed];
the Moon in the first house of Saturn, 22 minutes, 23 Jupiter[?], in the 24th Venus, according to this calculation.

Take, then, the Moon by its own account according to the completed/fulfilled course of the planet;
this is to be understood as the relation of the planet, that Saturn, in its own degree, measures;
according to this, the Moon by this account shows the aspect, and the planet is described by this means.

Other matters pertaining to the planet['s] influences, the planet is described in another way;
affections and the particular aspects produce changes according to how far removed the planet is from another;
the Moon has its [configuration] according to another [rule]; [so] that [its] aspect may be noted, let it be understood, etc.

And so the planet's degree is understood through the aspect, according to a certain method;
through two degrees, which are in their own triplicity, the aspect binds, so that the aspect is understood to be in that manner,
the aspect also being thus; and likewise this placement generates the aspect according to that method, being completed.

Good fortune in like manner is generated through this same method; this benevolent relation and aspect, in another manner, shows likewise;
of these, the majesty and benevolence, and likewise malice, gathered together, malice is understood [when combined];
the weaker/milder goodness and malice, together with these, is understood through this to be more combined.
